---
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<section id="what" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
  <p class="eyebrow">THE METHOD LIVES IN A RULEBOOK</p>
  <h2 id="what-heading">Start with the work you do.</h2>
  <p>Kerby loads a selected rulebook into your agent’s session. The rulebook supplies instructions and declares checks; supported hooks can enforce specific checks when installed.</p>
  <div class="books">
    <article><p class="eyebrow">01 / SOFTWARE ENGINEERING</p><h3>SWE</h3><p>An opinionated method for investigating, changing, and verifying software. Follow the work from its first question to its final evidence.</p><a class="cta" href={url('rulebooks/swe/')}>Explore the SWE guide →</a></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">02 / AGENT SKILLS</p><h3>Skill authoring</h3><p>Instructions that require a fresh evaluation of the exact skill text before presenting it as verified.</p><p class="coming">Guide coming · <a href="https://github.com/sorawit-w/kerby/tree/main/skills/kerby/rulebooks/skill-authoring">Read the source ↗</a></p></article>
  </div>
  <p class="authoring">Have a different kind of work? <a href="https://github.com/sorawit-w/kerby/blob/main/docs/AUTHORING-RULEBOOKS.md">Write a rulebook →</a></p>
</section>
<style>
section { border-top:1px solid var(--border); } h2 { margin:0 0 1rem; }
.books { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:3rem; margin-top:2.5rem; } article { border-top:1px solid var(--structure); padding-top:1.5rem; } h3 { font-size:1.8rem; margin:0; } article p { color:var(--secondary); } .coming,.authoring { font-size:.9rem; } .authoring { margin-top:2rem; }
@media(max-width:600px) { .books { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
